```java
@RestController
public class ProductController {
    private final ProductService productService;

    public ProductController(ProductService productService) {
        this.productService = productService; // explicit dependency, testable
    }

    @GetMapping("/products/{id}")
    public ResponseEntity<Product> getProduct(@PathVariable Long id) {
        // Spring parses the Long for us; missing product maps to 404, not 500
        return productService.findById(id)
            .map(ResponseEntity::ok)
            .orElse(ResponseEntity.notFound().build());
    }
}
```
The revised version fixes type parsing, returns a proper 404, and respects the controller to service to repository layering.

```java
// A reviewer dry-runs edge cases instead of only reading the happy path.
public class ReviewChecklistDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(safeDivide(10, 2)); // 5
        System.out.println(safeDivide(10, 0)); // 0 (guarded, instead of ArithmeticException)
    }

    static int safeDivide(int a, int b) {
        if (b == 0) return 0; // the correctness guard a reviewer would insist on
        return a / b;
    }
}
```
Running the awkward inputs in your head — zero, null, empty — is how reviewers catch bugs the author missed.

